From my experience with refactoring the entire `IRenderEngine`, I have a solution:

Screw this (in `ControlCore.cpp`):

```c++
 _renderer->TriggerFontChange(newDpi, _desiredFont, _actualFont);
```

Make it:

```cpp
_renderEngine->UpdateDpi();
// Create`a new `UpdateFont` method with more parameters only in DxEngine.
_renderEngine->UpdateFone(newDpi, _desiredFont, _actualFont, whatever we want to add);
```

This is totally possible in ControlCore, because it actually only care about DxEngine. See https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/pull/10615/files#r667455617

This is also what my PR is about: to make `renderer.cpp` thinner & give back the control to the actual engine.

> // Create a new `UpdateFont` method with more parameters only in DxEngine.
> _renderEngine->UpdateFone(newDpi, _desiredFont, _actualFont, whatever we want to add);

I like this. Would like to hear from @miniksa before proceeding though
